A||N||1||cscougar||How to remover Throttle Cable?||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||05-01-2000||05:25 PM||||I am trying to take a throttle cable loose from a wrecked 85 GT.  I have everything loose but the end that attaches to the accelerator pedal.  I took off the 2 bolts holding the pedal down but I still can't get to the end of the throttle cable under the dash.  Can anyone tell me the trick to unhooking this cable?<P>Thanks,<P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan86gt3.8||05-02-2000||07:48 PM||||What I had to do was take the 2 bolts that hold the pedal down and then turn it and wiggle it and move it around tilll the bar that goes up and over into the the center console, comes out.  I had to do it when i swapped my engine.  but thats how I had to do it.  Its imposible to do when that arm is over in the center channel, you have to wiggle it and move it and flip it around.  once its out of the center console its easy as pie.  Hope this helps, if I rambled too much or this did not make sinse to you right me an email and I will try and better explian it||||reg||1
